KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ braced default member initializer initializes class member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [class.base.init]/9-10, [dcl.init.list]: a braced default member
initializer of a class-typed non-static data member (`pair stored{-1, 7}`) must
initialize the member via its constructor.  CBMC default-constructs the member
instead, failing for a class with no default constructor ("found no match for
symbol 'pair'").  g++/clang++ accept it.  Flip to CORE once the braced default
member initializer is forwarded to the member's constructor.
